<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galo Plaza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1906–1987</span> · Also known as Galo Plaza Lasso</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galo Plaza Lasso was president of Ecuador from 1948 to 1952, the first in decades to complete a full term. His government encouraged the banana boom that made Ecuador the world's largest banana exporter and respected civil liberties. He later served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> as a mediator and was secretary general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/organization-of-american-states">Organization of American States</a> from 1968 to 1975.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galo-plaza.jpg" alt="Galo Plaza" width="320" height="529" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abbie Rowe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galo_Plaza_Lasso.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
